findings.description:
Line 23 calls the 10-15 ms overrun "the direct consequence" of the force loops, but there is no profile behind it. The measured tick body (`src/migratory_server/server.py:163-171`) includes more than `sim.step`:
- an awaited `sim_logger.write_tick`, enabled in `config/default.yaml:16-19`;
- `client_manager.broadcast`;
- `max_speeds`, a per-agent list comprehension (`src/migratory/engine/tick.py:60-63`);
- the per-agent query loop this slice keeps.

Step 2 is a manual five-minute observation of wall-clock ticks. Its pass/fail depends on costs this slice doesn't own, and it can't be repeated.

**Fix:** add a measurable check that isolates force computation, e.g. time `tick()` on a clustered 100-agent state before and after, with a numeric target. Keep the live run as a smoke test.
